<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulleungdo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ulleung Island</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulleungdo is a volcanic island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> (East Sea), about 120 kilometres off the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. It was the centre of the small state of Usan, which the Silla general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabu">Isabu</a> subdued in 512 according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samguk-sagi">Samguk sagi</a>. Under the Joseon dynasty it was long left uninhabited by official policy, and resettlement began in the 1880s; it now belongs to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-gyeongsang-province">North Gyeongsang Province</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulleungdo.jpg" alt="Ulleungdo" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA Landsat7 image · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulleung_island_from_above.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
